From 7495cf704fa9a625e0192e8fefce4561783b1fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:58:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/49] feat(gui): back up several folders in parallel (issue
 #6)

"Folders backed up in parallel" in the backup form, stored in config.json
("parallel", pushed to the service, so scheduled backups use it too), with
the recommended value (CPUs / 4) as a hint. runFoldersParallel runs the
folders of a multi-folder backup N at a time: one destination lock for the
batch, one VSS snapshot set for every folder, progress averaged and
statistics summed; the sequential path is unchanged.

Review fixes (Codex), CLI and GUI:
- Linux: folders on the same block device share one snapshot; a second one
  destroyed the first (its tracer looked like a leftover).
- The snapshot callback returns the folder failures, so Windows deletes the
  shadow copies right away.
- A snapshot that fails to be taken or released is never reported as success.
- e2e: the expected backup-id cleans the path like GenerateBackupID.
